{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"65b82f63-593c-4a37-ba1c-24efd4c8faca","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have audited [server.py](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py) and written the findings to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/ANSWER.md) without modifying the server.\n\n### Summary of Key Findings in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/ANSWER.md)\n\n1. **Auth, OAuth Discovery \u0026 Mid-Session `401`s ([`handle`](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py#L131-L169), [`Handler`](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py#L171-L218))**:\n   - `initialize` and `tools/list` succeed anonymously while advertising `capabilities.resources` and `add_note`. Clients that automatically call `resources/list` after `initialize` immediately hit a raw HTTP `401 {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`.\n   - `401` responses lack the required `WWW-Authenticate` header, and `GET /.well-known/oauth-*` discovery requests hit [`do_GET`](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py#L186-L187) and fail with `405 Method Not Allowed`.\n   - Wrong tokens or lowercase `bearer` schemes silently downgrade to `\"anon\"`.\n   - Error bodies like `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}` are not valid JSON-RPC error objects (`{code, message}`).\n\n2. **Protocol Negotiation \u0026 Notifications ([`handle`](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py#L131-L169))**:\n   - `initialize` ignores `params.protocolVersion` and hardcodes `\"2025-06-18\"`, causing `\"2024-11-05\"` / `\"2025-03-26\"` clients to disconnect.\n   - Any notification other than `notifications/initialized` (such as `notifications/cancelled` or `notifications/roots/list_changed`) returns `200 OK` with a JSON-RPC `-32601` error (`id: null`) instead of `202 Accepted` with no body.\n\n3. **Streamable HTTP Transport, Sessions \u0026 Batching ([`Handler`](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py#L171-L218))**:\n   - `Mcp-Session-Id` is never stored or validated, and [`do_DELETE`](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py#L189-L190) does not invalidate sessions (terminated sessions never return `404`).\n   - JSON-RPC batching (removed in `2025-06-18`) drops per-item HTTP status codes (turning `401` into a `200` batch element), returns `200 []` for notification-only or empty batches, and skips `Mcp-Session-Id` generation on `initialize`.\n   - Query strings on `/mcp` cause `404`s, `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` reads 0 bytes, CORS/`OPTIONS` is unsupported (`501`), and non-dict JSON bodies or `params` crash the handler with `AttributeError`.\n\n4. **Tool Schemas, `structuredContent` \u0026 Execution ([`TOOLS`](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py#L25-L73), [`call_tool`](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py#L101-L128))**:\n   - `add_note` indexes `args[\"title\"]` and `args[\"body\"]` directly while [`handle`](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py#L161-L164) only catches `ValueError`; missing arguments raise an uncaught `KeyError` and drop the HTTP connection.\n   - `search_notes` declares `\"outputSchema\": {\"type\": \"object\"}` with no `properties` (rejected by strict schema validators like Gemini/Codex), returns a JSON array in `content[0].text` vs. an object in `structuredContent`, computes `total` after slicing `hits[:limit]`, and slices `n[\"body\"]` using an index computed against `n[\"title\"] + \" \" + n[\"body\"]`.\n   - `get_note` reports missing notes as a JSON-RPC `-32602` error instead of a tool result with `isError: true`.\n   - `add_note` does not enforce `minLength: 1` or string types, allowing notes with `title: \"\"` that subsequently fail client-side `outputSchema` validation on `get_note`.\n\n5. **Resources ([`handle`](file:///tmp/h-grZN9R/server.py#L148-L155))**:\n   - `resources/read` ignores `params.uri` and always returns `notes://guide`.\n","duration_seconds":346.582892,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":58218,"output_tokens":24279,"thinking_tokens":17643,"cache_read_tokens":236041,"total_tokens":82497}}}
